## Problem Statement

The backend now emits `PlayerJoined` and `PlayerDisconnected` events (implemented in ensayo_quest-8lv), but the frontend:
1. Ignores these events in the reducer
2. Has no UI to display who is in the room
3. Has no state to track participants

For multiplayer scenarios, users need to see:
- Who is in the room
- Who is currently connected vs disconnected
- Whose turn it is

## Effect API Reference

Events are defined in the shared protocol:

```typescript
// shared/src/RoomProtocol.ts (or apps/api/src/domain/RoomProtocol.ts)
type PlayerJoined = {
  type: "PlayerJoined";
  playerId: string;
  sessionId: string;
  timestamp: number;
};

type PlayerDisconnected = {
  type: "PlayerDisconnected";
  playerId: string;
  sessionId: string;
  timestamp: number;
};
```

**Review Effect Source:**
- `effect/packages/experimental/src/EventLog.ts` for event consumption patterns
- Backend implementation: `apps/api/src/durable-objects/RoomDurableObject.ts` lines 384-400, 470-486

## Implementation

### 1. Add participant state

```typescript
// apps/web/eventlog/RoomEventReducer.ts
type Participant = {
  playerId: string;
  sessionId: string;
  isConnected: boolean;
  joinedAt: number;
};

type RoomState = {
  // ... existing fields
  participants: Participant[];
  currentPlayerId: string | null;  // whose turn
};
```

### 2. Handle events in reducer

```typescript
case "PlayerJoined":
  return {
    ...state,
    participants: [
      ...state.participants.filter(p => p.sessionId !== event.sessionId),
      { playerId: event.playerId, sessionId: event.sessionId, isConnected: true, joinedAt: event.timestamp }
    ]
  };

case "PlayerDisconnected":
  return {
    ...state,
    participants: state.participants.map(p =>
      p.sessionId === event.sessionId ? { ...p, isConnected: false } : p
    )
  };
```

### 3. Create ParticipantList component

```tsx
const ParticipantList = ({ participants, currentPlayerId }: Props) => (
  <div className="participant-list">
    <h3>Players</h3>
    {participants.map(p => (
      <div key={p.sessionId} className={p.isConnected ? "connected" : "disconnected"}>
        {p.playerId === currentPlayerId && "▶ "}
        {p.playerId}
        {!p.isConnected && " (disconnected)"}
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
);
```

