## Architecture Reference

**BEFORE IMPLEMENTATION**: Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` - this issue implements Invariants #2 and #6.

| Invariant | Rule |
|-----------|------|
| #2 | All commands are idempotent via requestId |
| #6 | DO alarms are guarded by idempotency |

## Problem Statement

Commands lack idempotency protection:
- `SubmitTurn` has no `requestId` field
- `GenerateNpcTurn` has no idempotency guard
- DO alarms can fire up to 7 times (at-least-once semantics)
- No guard in `alarm()` handler before sending commands

## Existing Pattern (queue consumer)

The queue consumer already implements idempotency correctly:

```typescript
// apps/api/src/index.ts:216-222
const alreadyProcessed = yield* db.isMessageProcessed(message.id);
if (alreadyProcessed) { message.ack(); return; }
yield* consumer.handle(message.body);
yield* db.markMessageProcessed(message.id);
```

Apply this same pattern to commands.

## Implementation

### 1. Add requestId to schemas

```typescript
class SubmitTurn extends Schema.TaggedRequest<SubmitTurn>()(
  "SubmitTurn",
  { failure: Schema.String, success: Schema.Struct({ turnId: Schema.String }) },
  {
    playerId: Schema.String,
    transcript: Schema.String,
    requestId: Schema.String,  // NEW
    // ...
  }
) {}
```

### 2. Create idempotency tables

```sql
CREATE TABLE turn_requests (
  room_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  request_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  turn_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  created_at INTEGER,
  PRIMARY KEY (room_id, request_id)
);

CREATE TABLE alarm_processing (
  npc_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  step_index INTEGER NOT NULL,
  scheduled_at INTEGER NOT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (npc_id, step_index, scheduled_at)
);
```

### 3. Guard alarm() handler

```typescript
async alarm() {
  const pending = await loadPendingNpc();
  if (!pending) return;

  const alreadyFired = await db.checkAlarmFired(pending.npcId, pending.stepIndex);
  if (alreadyFired) return;  // Idempotent skip

  await db.markAlarmFired({ ... });
  await actor.send(new GenerateNpcTurn({ ... }));
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] SubmitTurn, GenerateNpcTurn have requestId field
- [ ] turn_requests table exists and is checked
- [ ] alarm_processing table exists and is checked
- [ ] alarm() handler guards before sending commands
- [ ] Test: 7 alarm retries → only one NPC turn generated
- [ ] Test: network retry of SubmitTurn → returns cached turnId

